  "source_review": [
    "Finite, UTC-representable numeric dates are normalized before comparison; bool, invalid, non-finite and overflowing dates cannot establish chronology. Numeric strings and epoch zero remain supported.",
    "A first snapshot is selected even with unknown time. Afterwards known dates outrank unknown dates, only strictly newer known dates replace known dates, and equal/incomparable different snapshots retain current.",
    "Fingerprint excludes update_time. Identical content can raise but cannot lower or erase its known time; no extra snapshot is required.",
    "Title, current snapshot and selected timestamp change together. Candidate snapshots, revisions and evidence remain; search/discover continue to use selected current.",
    "Additive snapshot_selection describes each processed conversation, including duplicate IDs/ZIP ordering. Existing return keys and already_imported database no-op remain.",
    "Legacy schema 1 invalid stored times are normalized for selection. No migration or automatic reconstruction of previously corrupted chronology is claimed.",
    "The single database transaction rolls back selection and history together after a later malformed conversation.",
    "Four expected red failures are real current-snapshot/title/freshness regressions in public import_file, not absent response fields or import/harness errors."
  ],
